        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "First, load the graph into the in-memory graph server so you can run the graph algorithms.",
          "",
          "Run the first %python-pgx paragraph, which uses the built-in session object to read the graph into memory from the database and creates a PgXGraph object that handles the loaded graph."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%python-pgx",
          "",
          "GRAPH_NAME=\"AIRTIME_GRAPH\"",
          "# try getting the graph from the in-memory graph server",
          "graph = session.get_graph(GRAPH_NAME)",
          "# if it does not exist read it into memory",
          "if (graph == None) :",
          "    session.read_graph_by_name(GRAPH_NAME, \"pg_pgql\")",
          "    print(\"Graph \"+ GRAPH_NAME + \" successfully loaded\")",
          "    graph = session.get_graph(GRAPH_NAME)",
          "else :",
          "    print(\"Graph '\"+ GRAPH_NAME + \"' already loaded\")"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "raw",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "Next, execute the paragraph that queries and displays 100 graph elements.",
          "",
          "This PGQL query fetches the first 100 elements of the graph and displays them.",
          "The **MATCH** clause specifies a graph pattern.",
          "",
          "- (s) is the source node",
          "",
          "- [t] is an edge",
          "",
          "- -> indicates the edge direction, that is, from the source s to a destination d",
          "",
          "- (d) is the destination node",
          "",
          "The **LIMIT** clause specifies the maximum of elements that the query should return.",
          "",
          "See the [PGQL site](https://pgql-lang.org/) and specification for more details on the syntax and features of the language.",
          "The Getting Started notebook folder also has a tutorial on PGQL."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%pgql-pgx",
          "/* Query and visualize 100 elements (nodes and edges) of AIRTIME_GRAPH */",
          "SELECT *",
          "FROM MATCH (s)-[t]->(d) ON airtime_graph",
          "LIMIT 100"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "visualization",
        "visualizationConfig": "[{\"visualization\": {\"vertexLabelProperty\": \"ACCOUNT_ID\", \"layout\": \"concentric\", \"version\": 9}}]",
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "This shows the use of bind parameters in a query. You enter the account ID when you run the query.",
          "",
          "Enter **534** as the account id, and then execute the paragraph."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%pgql-pgx",
          "/* Check if there are any circular airtime-transfer chains of between 1 and 5 hops starting from the user-supplied account # */",
          "SELECT v,e,v2",
          "FROM MATCH ANY (a)-[:TRANSFERS]->{1,5}(b) ON airtime_graph ONE ROW PER STEP (v,e,v2)",
          "WHERE a.account_id=${account_id} AND id(a) = id(b)"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "visualization",
        "visualizationConfig": "[{\"visualization\": {\"vertexLabelProperty\": \"ACCOUNT_ID\", \"version\": 9}}]",
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[{\"type\": \"TextBox\", \"name\": \"account_id\", \"displayName\": null, \"defaultValue\": \"\", \"argument\": null, \"isHidden\": false, \"isProgrammatic\": false}]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{\"account_id\": \"534\"}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "Use PGQL to find the 10 accounts with the most transfers.",
          "",
          "PGQL has built-in functions **IN_DEGREE** and **OUT_DEGREE**, which return the number of incoming and outgoing edges of a node. So we can use them in this query.",
          "",
          "Run the paragraph with the following query."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%pgql-pgx",
          "/* List 10 accounts with the most number of airtime transfers (that is, incoming + outgoing edges) */",
          "SELECT a.account_id, (in_degree(a) + out_degree(a)) AS num_transfers",
          "FROM MATCH (a) ON airtime_graph",
          "ORDER BY num_transfers DESC",
          "LIMIT 10"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "table",
        "visualizationConfig": "[{\"visualization\": {\"version\": 9}}]",
        "hideCode": false,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%md",
          "Review the accounts with the highest degree. The sample data includes account 934 as a starting point for a circular airtime-transfer investigation. Many transfers are a reason to look closer, not proof of abuse. The next query checks four-hop cycles with ONE ROW PER STEP so you can see each vertex and edge."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "html",
        "visualizationConfig": null,
        "hideCode": true,
        "hideResult": false,
        "hideGutter": true,
        "hideVizConfig": false,
        "hideInIFrame": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "forms": "[]",
        "relations": [],
        "dynamicFormParams": "{}",
        "result": null
      },
      {
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sizeX": 0,
        "width": 12,
        "title": null,
        "hasTitle": false,
        "message": [
          "%pgql-pgx",
          "/* Check if there are any circular airtime-transfer chains of length 4 from account 934 */",
          "SELECT v,e,v2",
          "FROM MATCH ALL (a)-[:TRANSFERS]->{4}(b) ON airtime_graph ONE ROW PER STEP (v,e,v2)",
          "WHERE a.account_id=934 AND id(a) = id(b)",
          "LIMIT 100"
        ],
        "selectedVisualization": "visualization",
        "visualizationConfig": "[{\"visualization\": {\"filters\": [{\"_id\": 1661441592752, \"component\": \"vertex\", \"type\": \"styling\", \"target\": \"vertex\", \"enabled\": true, \"conditions\": {\"operator\": \"and\", \"conditions\": [{\"property\": \"ACCOUNT_ID\", \"operator\": \"=\", \"value\": \"934\"}]}, \"properties\": {\"colors\": [\"red\"], \"sizes\": [17]}, \"aggregation\": []}], \"vertexLabelProperty\": \"ACCOUNT_ID\", \"version\": 9}}]",
